clk: mediatek: mt6797: stop the GPU mux reparenting onto the system PLLs

CLK_TOP_MUX_MFG is declared with MUX_GATE(), which sets CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT
and leaves reparenting enabled. Two of its four parents — syspll_d3 and
univpll_d3 — are FACTOR() children of mainpll and univpll, and FACTOR() also
carries CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT. clk_mux_determine_rate_flags() is therefore
allowed to satisfy a GPU operating point by switching the GPU onto a system
PLL branch and reprogramming that PLL, which on this SoC clocks the AXI bus,
MSDC, I2C and the UARTs.

Measured on a Gemini PDA (MT6797, Mali-T880, panfrost + devfreq): requesting
the 610 MHz GPU OPP moved CLK_CFG_5[25:24] from 1 (mfgpll_ck) to 2 and left
MFGPLL_CON0 = 0x0, i.e. the GPU PLL switched off and the GPU clocked from a
system PLL branch — while devfreq and the clock framework both reported
610 MHz. The next rate change from that state hard-locked CPUs and timed out
every unrelated bus master on the die; only the watchdog recovered it. OPPs at
or below 520 MHz keep the mux on mfgpll_ck and survived 60 consecutive
transitions unharmed.

CLK_SET_RATE_NO_REPARENT keeps the rate request on the current parent, so it
propagates to MFGPLL — the only PLL a GPU operating point has any business
moving.

--- a/drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt6797.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt6797.c
@@ -333,7 +333,29 @@
 	MUX_GATE(CLK_TOP_MUX_PWM, "pwm_sel", pwm_parents, 0x0050, 0, 3, 7),
 	MUX_GATE(CLK_TOP_MUX_VDEC, "vdec_sel", vdec_parents, 0x0050, 8, 3, 15),
 	MUX_GATE(CLK_TOP_MUX_VENC, "venc_sel", venc_parents, 0x0050, 16, 2, 23),
-	MUX_GATE(CLK_TOP_MUX_MFG, "mfg_sel", mfg_parents, 0x0050, 24, 2, 31),
+	/*
+	 * The GPU's clock mux must never reparent. Two of its four parents,
+	 * syspll_d3 and univpll_d3, are FACTOR() children of mainpll and
+	 * univpll — the PLLs that clock the AXI bus, MSDC, I2C and the UARTs —
+	 * and FACTOR() carries CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT. So a GPU operating point
+	 * that the current MFGPLL rate cannot satisfy is served, entirely
+	 * legally, by switching the GPU onto a system PLL and reprogramming
+	 * that PLL for the whole SoC.
+	 *
+	 * Measured on a Gemini PDA (MT6797, Mali-T880): requesting the 610 MHz
+	 * GPU OPP moved CLK_CFG_5[25:24] from 1 (mfgpll_ck) to 2 and left
+	 * MFGPLL_CON0 = 0x0 — the GPU PLL switched off and the GPU clocked
+	 * from a system PLL branch, while devfreq and the clock framework both
+	 * reported 610 MHz. The next rate change from that state hard-locked
+	 * CPUs and timed out every unrelated bus master on the die (I2C, SDIO,
+	 * eMMC), reclaimed only by the watchdog. Operating points at or below
+	 * 520 MHz stay on MFGPLL and are stable across many transitions.
+	 *
+	 * CLK_SET_RATE_NO_REPARENT keeps a rate request on the current parent,
+	 * so it reaches MFGPLL — the only PLL a GPU operating point may move.
+	 */
+	MUX_GATE_FLAGS(CLK_TOP_MUX_MFG, "mfg_sel", mfg_parents, 0x0050, 24, 2,
+		       31, CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT | CLK_SET_RATE_NO_REPARENT),
 	MUX_GATE(CLK_TOP_MUX_CAMTG, "camtg_sel", camtg, 0x0060, 0, 2, 7),
 	MUX_GATE(CLK_TOP_MUX_UART, "uart_sel", uart_parents, 0x0060, 8, 1, 15),
 	MUX_GATE(CLK_TOP_MUX_SPI, "spi_sel", spi_parents, 0x0060, 16, 2, 23),
